date-released: "2026-10-06"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous verification laboratory connecting the AB-Cloud programme to the
  Dirac equation. Fourteen tests (D1-D14) establish that the clean alpha = 1/2
  Hofstadter model is a lattice discretization of the massless Dirac equation
  (v_F = 2t, E_1 x L -> 4 pi, fourfold chiral zero tower, Berry phase pi,
  relativistic Landau levels, Klein supertansmission, Zitterbewegung at
  omega = 2E); that zeta-zero-decorated vortex phases lift the bulk statistics
  to the GUE value while preserving the chiral skeleton to machine precision;
  that the index is restored by a Jackiw-Rossi wall surviving the full zeta
  background (contrast 7e6) and staying pinned along the whole Connes orbit;
  that the Montgomery/Odlyzko statistics are carried dynamically by the vortex
  channel (pair correlation, transport protection, two-point form factor with
  an exact unit plateau at t ~ 1e5); and that the AB-Cloud coding phase is
  exactly the Berry-Keating/Connes conjugation-action staircase — the BK
  ladder extends to the infinite limit at fixed density with the trace comb
  sharpening into the Connes delta train. Python canonical suite plus an
  independent Julia cross-implementation; all 96 checks pass. Includes two
  monograph editions (EN/RU LaTeX + DOCX), a self-contained LaTeX monograph with 600-dpi figures for each of the fourteen tests, publication figures, infographics and
  two interactive web applications.
